Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:32:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: the frame at the window's size, anamorphic when
 asked

PS3RECOMP_VK_SCALE_XY=<x>,<y> scales the two axes of the internal resolution
apart. PS3RECOMP_VK_SCALE_FIT=fit|fill takes the scale from the window's size
in pixels (the display mode's, fullscreen) times PS3RECOMP_VK_SCALE: fit is
the largest 16:9 frame the window holds, fill scales each axis to the window,
for a title whose cameras were widened to the window's aspect.
rsx_vulkan_set_stretch (or PS3RECOMP_VK_STRETCH=1) presents the frame over
the whole window instead of with bars, and rsx_vulkan_output_size gives the
window's drawable size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.h b/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.h
index dcb2e6ca..03e73616 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.h
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_vulkan_backend.h
@@ -80,6 +80,8 @@ int  rsx_vulkan_backend_pump_messages(void);
 void rsx_vulkan_set_display(const char* mode, int w, int h, int hz);
 void rsx_vulkan_set_present(const char* mode);
 int  rsx_vulkan_display_sizes(int (*out)[2], int max);
+void rsx_vulkan_set_stretch(int on);
+int  rsx_vulkan_output_size(int* w, int* h);
 
 /* Read the frame back to host memory (and to PS3RECOMP_VK_DUMP if set), and
  * show it in the window if there is one. Same as _present_begin() followed
